pages=[
('Contents',['This report follows and expands the supplied Project Report Submission Template. It covers the proposal, deliverables, model questions, important findings, resources, individual details, and milestones. Word page numbers are generated in the footer.','Sections: 1 Executive summary; 2 Project brief; 3 Problem and scope; 4 Questions and deliverables; 5 Dataset and fields; 6 Quality assessment; 7 Exploratory analysis; 8 Feature and target design; 9 Methodology; 10 Candidates; 11 Evaluation; 12 Results; 13 Findings; 14 Application design; 15 Run and deployment; 16 Risks and limitations; 17 Milestones and resources; 18 Individual details, references, glossary.']),
('Executive Summary',[f'This project estimates residential listing prices in Indian lakhs from the supplied House Price.csv. The source contains {M["data_rows_raw"]:,} rows and 12 columns. Exact duplicate removal leaves {M["data_rows_after_duplicate_removal"]:,} records. TARGET(PRICE_IN_LACS) is the prediction target.',f'A fixed 80/20 random split (seed 42) compared a median baseline, Ridge regression, Random Forest, and Extra Trees. Random Forest was selected on test MAE of ₹{M["models"]["Random forest"]["mae_lakhs"]:.2f} lakhs; its RMSE is ₹{M["models"]["Random forest"]["rmse_lakhs"]:.2f} lakhs and R² is {M["models"]["Random forest"]["r2"]:.3f}. The large gap between MAE and RMSE reflects a long, influential upper tail.', 'The result supports an educational estimator, not certified valuation. Extreme area and coordinate values, unknown collection dates, repeated locations, and absent sale outcomes constrain confidence. A future release should use time- or geography-based validation, investigate flagged rows, and report segment errors.']),
('Project Brief',['Project type is supervised regression. Users enter property characteristics and receive a point estimate of recorded listing price. The app also provides descriptive views of the supplied sample.', 'The motivation is to help buyers, sellers, or analysts create an initial comparison point. The target records listed prices; the files do not establish completed transaction prices. The model therefore cannot claim to predict a negotiated sale or current market value.', 'The workflow reviews the data dictionary and CSV, profiles data quality, removes exact duplicates, prepares mixed categorical and numeric fields, compares simple and tree-based candidates, selects by test MAE, persists the full preprocessing and prediction pipeline, and exposes it through Streamlit. The supplied files provide no dataset URL, collection date, or transaction outcomes.']),
('Problem Statement and Scope',['The target is continuous and positive. One lakh equals ₹100,000; the app displays output in lakhs to match the source. Inputs include poster, construction/readiness, RERA status, room count and type, area, address, longitude, and latitude.', 'The intended user is a learner or analyst exploring structured prediction. In scope are data profiling, baseline comparison, one fixed holdout, a local app, and documentation. Out of scope are scraping, live feeds, legal verification, mortgage advice, investment recommendations, and certified appraisal.', 'The model captures associations in observational listings, not causes. Price can depend on condition, floor, amenities, exact micro-location, date, title status, and negotiation, which are absent. Users should compare recent local listings and seek qualified valuation for consequential decisions.']),
('Questions and Deliverables',['The experiment asks how accurately the supplied fields predict recorded price on a random holdout; whether nonlinear ensembles improve on a constant and a linear benchmark; and how typical absolute error compares with tail-sensitive squared error.', 'Exploratory questions include whether price is skewed, which categories and locations occur, whether records are missing or duplicated, and whether physical values appear plausible. These checks do not establish market representativeness.', 'Deliverables are the VS Code folder, Streamlit interface, training script, dependency list, source CSV copy, fitted pipeline, JSON metrics, and this MDD. The data description and template are retained in reports. Evidence includes schema checks, duplicate counts, summary statistics, split design, candidate scores, and a working local workflow. No external test, uncertainty intervals, temporal evaluation, or causal analysis is included.']),
('Dataset and Field Definitions',['The data description says each row is a residential listing and names TARGET(PRICE_IN_LACS) as the target. The local file is data/house_price.csv. No public source URL or collection date accompanies the files; provenance beyond the supplied attachments is unresolved.', 'There are 11 candidate predictors. POSTED_BY, BHK_OR_RK, and ADDRESS are nominal categories. Four construction/readiness/RERA/resale flags are binary. BHK_NO. is a discrete room count. SQUARE_FT, LONGITUDE, and LATITUDE are numeric.', 'ADDRESS is treated as a categorical token, not natural-language text. It has 6,880 unique values after duplicate removal. Rare categories are grouped. The supplied RERA meaning and coordinate names are accepted without independent regulatory or geographic verification. No currency conversion date is available.'],['Field group','Fields','Treatment'],[['Categorical','POSTED_BY; BHK_OR_RK; ADDRESS','One-hot; rare levels grouped'],['Binary','UNDER_CONSTRUCTION; RERA; READY_TO_MOVE; RESALE','Numeric flags'],['Numeric','BHK_NO.; SQUARE_FT; LONGITUDE; LATITUDE','Median impute and scale'],['Target','TARGET(PRICE_IN_LACS)','Log fit; output in lakhs']]),
('Data Quality Assessment',[f'The initial file has {M["data_rows_raw"]:,} rows, 12 columns, and zero null cells. Exact comparison found {M["duplicate_rows_removed"]:,} duplicated rows, leaving {M["data_rows_after_duplicate_removal"]:,} distinct records. Duplicate removal precedes the split to avoid identical rows crossing partitions.',f'Area has a median of {M["area_median_sqft"]:,.1f} sq ft, a 99th percentile of {M["area_p99_sqft"]:,.1f}, and a maximum of {M["area_max_sqft"]:,.1f}. The maximum is far outside ordinary scale and suggests unit, parsing, or source error. Price ranges from ₹{M["target_min_lakhs"]:.2f}L to ₹{M["target_max_lakhs"]:,.0f}L; mean ₹{M["target_mean_lakhs"]:,.2f}L exceeds median ₹{M["target_median_lakhs"]:,.2f}L.', 'Longitude spans −37.71 to 59.91 and latitude −121.76 to 152.96 in the initial profile, including values inconsistent with ordinary India coordinates. This project does not guess at geographic deletion rules; it preserves rows and flags the issue for source-based review.', 'The fitted pipeline still includes median/mode imputers for future incomplete values. The app limits entered area for usability, but this does not alter training data.']),
('Exploratory Analysis',['Prices are strongly right-skewed: median ₹61.75L, mean ₹141.71L, maximum ₹30,000L. Squared-error metrics heavily weight expensive misses; central and tail behavior must be read together.', 'Typical area is near 1,173 sq ft, while the top 1% begins around 5,400 sq ft. Extreme observations distort ordinary plots. The Streamlit chart filters above the 99th price percentile for display only; source rows are not changed.', 'Three poster categories, two property types, and thousands of locations create uneven representation. National metrics can hide poor performance for specific cities or price bands. Recommended follow-up includes log price distributions, price per square foot by city, and error by city, BHK, and price band. Mapping should wait until coordinate validation.']),
('Feature and Target Design',['All 11 available predictors are used; no target-derived field enters the model. Categorical strings are stripped and normalized. Split happens before preprocessing fit, so learned encodings and imputations use training rows only.', 'The full ADDRESS is one-hot encoded. This captures repeated local patterns but may not generalize to new areas. A later design could split city and locality from address and compare under geography-aware partitions.', 'The target receives log1p during fitting and expm1 at inference; scores remain in lakhs. The transform reduces influence from large values but does not remove outliers or calibrate uncertainty.', 'Numeric inputs receive median imputation and sparse-compatible scaling. Scaling is not essential for trees, but it supports a consistent pipeline and Ridge benchmark. The serialized object carries preprocessing with the estimator.']),
('Development Methodology',['src/train_model.py loads the CSV, drops exact duplicates, normalizes strings, defines the feature list, and creates an 80% training and 20% test split with seed 42. The test portion is not used to fit candidates.', 'A ColumnTransformer applies imputation and OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown="infrequent_if_exist", min_frequency=5) to categories, and median imputation plus StandardScaler(with_mean=False) to numeric fields. TransformedTargetRegressor applies log1p and expm1.', 'Candidates are a training median baseline, Ridge(alpha=10), Random Forest (180 trees, minimum leaf 2), and Extra Trees (220 trees, minimum leaf 2). Ensemble seeds are fixed; local parallel fitting is enabled.', 'Selection uses the lowest test MAE. Repeatedly selecting from a fixed holdout can overfit evaluation decisions. A mature evaluation should tune only inside training folds and retain an untouched geographic or temporal test.']),
('Model Candidates',['The median baseline predicts the training median for every row and checks whether features add signal. Ridge is a regularized linear benchmark for an additive relationship in transformed one-hot and numeric features.', 'Random Forest averages many decision trees and can represent nonlinear interactions among size, location, and configuration. The chosen configuration uses 180 estimators, minimum leaf size 2, and a fixed seed.', 'Extra Trees randomizes split thresholds more strongly and offers a different ensemble comparison. It uses 220 estimators and the same minimum leaf size. Both tree candidates share preprocessing and target transformation.', 'Random Forest wins this holdout by MAE. No hyperparameter search was performed, so the report does not claim global optimization. Retraining regenerates the candidate comparison and fitted artifact.']),
('Evaluation Design',['There are 23,240 training rows and 5,810 test rows after duplicate removal. The random split is reproducible but assumes independent, exchangeable records. Nearby listings or common market periods can appear in both sets.', 'MAE is average absolute error in lakhs and drives selection. Median AE describes the middle absolute error. RMSE weights large errors more. R² can be negative when worse than predicting test mean. MdAPE is median absolute percentage error and is unstable near zero; targets reach ₹0.25L.', 'Scores are from one seed and one split; no confidence intervals or repeat-split variability are available. Before broader claims, calculate errors by city, price quantile, property type, BHK, and area band.', 'These scores describe a random holdout, not future forecasting or generalization to new cities and market conditions.']),
('Measured Results',[f'Random Forest test MAE is ₹{M["models"]["Random forest"]["mae_lakhs"]:.2f}L, median AE ₹{M["models"]["Random forest"]["median_absolute_error_lakhs"]:.2f}L, RMSE ₹{M["models"]["Random forest"]["rmse_lakhs"]:.2f}L, R² {M["models"]["Random forest"]["r2"]:.3f}, and MdAPE {M["models"]["Random forest"]["median_absolute_percentage_error_pct"]:.1f}%.', 'Median baseline MAE is ₹111.01L. Ridge MAE is ₹128.23L and its RMSE/R² are very poor on this split. Extra Trees has MAE ₹42.52L and R² 0.621. Random Forest lowers MAE about 67.6% against the constant baseline.', 'RMSE is roughly eleven times MAE, indicating a small number of expensive or anomalous misses contributes large squared error. These values are generated into reports/model_metrics.json; data or code changes require rerun and report refresh.'],['Model','MAE L','Median AE L','RMSE L','R²','MdAPE %'],[['Median baseline','111.01','29.00','745.01','−0.014','48.3'],['Ridge','128.23','17.55','2,845.59','−13.788','29.6'],['Random Forest','35.97','9.13','400.34','0.707','15.4'],['Extra Trees','42.52','9.23','455.69','0.621','15.8']]),
('Findings and Interpretation',['The tree ensembles improve typical error over the constant baseline, indicating listing characteristics and location carry predictive signal. Random Forest ranks first by MAE for this fixed split.', 'MAE ₹35.97L is substantial relative to median price ₹61.75L. MdAPE 15.4% describes typical proportional error but hides the tail. RMSE ₹400.34L indicates substantial instability among large or anomalous cases.', 'Ridge’s poor score shows this particular regularized linear configuration is not a good primary model; it does not prove all linear approaches fail. Robust losses and different feature design could change the comparison.', 'The app avoids causal feature claims. Future work can add permutation importance and partial dependence with caveats, segment metrics, and prediction intervals. Correlated fields may divide or distort importance.']),
('Streamlit Application Design',['app.py provides Estimate a property, Explore the dataset, and About the model tabs. The estimate tab gathers inputs, loads the saved pipeline, creates a row in training feature order, and displays price in lakhs.', 'Address options come from known dataset values, with representative coordinates prefilled; users can edit coordinates. This simplifies known categories but does not provide free-form address discovery. Unknown categories remain supported by the encoder.', 'The explorer displays row count, missing values, median price and area, distinct locations, a BHK price chart, poster counts, source table, and CSV download. The chart omits rows above the 99th price percentile only for legibility.', 'A missing model message includes the training command. Point estimates are labelled educational and explicitly lack uncertainty intervals and market updates.']),
('Run and Deployment Guide',['Open House_Price_Prediction in VS Code. In PowerShell create and activate a virtual environment, install requirements.txt, run python src/train_model.py, then streamlit run app.py. README and VS Code task/launch files repeat the workflow.', 'Training writes models/house_price_pipeline.joblib and reports/model_metrics.json. The app expects these along with data/house_price.csv. A clean checkout can recreate the artifact from bundled data.', 'For a hosted demo, keep secrets outside source control, limit data exposure, check dependency compatibility, and protect access. The app needs no external API or database.', 'Joblib objects are Python and library-version sensitive and must only come from trusted sources. The project pins scikit-learn 1.6.1 and Streamlit 1.50.0. Retraining after version or data changes should regenerate scores and report.']),
('Risks, Fairness, and Limitations',['Extreme area and coordinate values can indicate corrupted records. The model can learn their patterns and return unreliable estimates. The source does not establish valid coordinate bounds, area units for anomalies, or whether repeated records are genuinely duplicate listings.', 'Coverage is unknown; some states, cities, channels, and prices may be overrepresented. Random holdout shares those patterns and can overstate performance in thinly represented markets. Evaluate subgroup counts and errors before wider use.', 'Housing prices are consequential. The app is not legal, lending, insurance, or investment advice. It has no uncertainty interval and does not reflect market change. Seek qualified review for important decisions.', 'Location and listing fields can proxy for socioeconomic or protected attributes. No fairness audit, privacy review, or regulatory assessment has been completed. Do not use the estimate to deny access to services.', 'Mitigations are visible educational-use language, no guarantees, retained source files, transparent holdout limits, and future source validation, grouped evaluation, and uncertainty estimates.']),
('Milestones and Resources',['The template asks for milestones but no dates were supplied. Source review, data checks, candidate comparison, saved model, Streamlit app, and report are complete. These steps are reproducible in the project files.', 'Next obtain authoritative dataset provenance, confirm units and coordinate convention, review flagged records, and build geography/time-aware partitions. Then use training-only cross-validation, tune a bounded candidate set, and report subgroup errors and calibration.', 'Resources are Python, pandas, NumPy, scikit-learn, joblib, Streamlit, VS Code, supplied CSV, and two supplied Word documents. No database or inference service is required.', 'The dataset URL is absent and must not be guessed. Add it to README and this report if known. Model comparison and dependency versions are in model_metrics.json and requirements.txt.'],['Milestone','Status','Evidence / next action'],[['Read sources and profile data','Complete','Data dictionary and audit'],['Train and compare candidates','Complete','Script and metrics JSON'],['Build Streamlit interface','Complete','app.py and VS Code config'],['Source validation and grouped split','Planned','Confirm source and repair flags'],['Segment review and uncertainty','Planned','City/price errors and intervals']]),
('Individual Details, References, and Glossary',['The template requires individual details, but none were supplied. Complete before submission: Name: ____________________; Email: ____________________; Phone: ____________________. No identity or contact details have been invented.', 'The template makes papers optional. No external paper is cited because only the supplied files provide project-specific evidence. Add bibliography entries if the course rubric requires them. The modeling implementation and metric names are given in the project source and reports.', 'Glossary: BHK means bedroom, hall, kitchen; RK means room, kitchen; RERA is the approval flag as supplied; lakh is ₹100,000; MAE is mean absolute error; median AE is median absolute error; RMSE is root mean squared error; R² is coefficient of determination; MdAPE is median absolute percentage error; holdout is data kept out of fitting for evaluation.', 'Submission checklist: complete personal information; add source URL if known; verify final page count in Word; rerun training after source changes; open the app and make a sample estimate.'])
]
